# Fix Mermaid erDiagram chunk load failures

## Problem
After PROD redeploy, Mermaid lazy-loads `erDiagram-*.js` with a prior build hash. The SPA catch-all returns `index.html` (200 HTML) for missing `/assets/*`, so `import()` fails and the NodeView shows the raw Vite error.

## Approach
1. Return 404 for missing `/assets/` and other static extensions — never HTML fallback.
2. `Cache-Control: no-cache` for `index.html`; long immutable cache for hashed `/assets/*`.
3. Mermaid NodeView: reload-friendly chunk-load error UX; sync `editable` on TipTap `update` as well as `transaction`.

## Out of scope
- Eager-bundling all Mermaid diagram types.
